WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.160 --> 00:00:11.760
Millions of Americans live in distressed communities, where poverty rates are high and levels of education and workforce participation are low.

00:00:12.240 --> 00:00:16.440
These areas face many challenges but a big one is their lack of access to capital.

00:00:16.620 --> 00:00:19.940
These communities have hopes and dreams, but no one is investing in them.

00:00:20.100 --> 00:00:28.220
The new Opportunity Zone program can help. It had governors designate 25% of their low income census tracts to be "opportunity zones"

00:00:28.220 --> 00:00:35.000
— more than 8,700 nationwide — and it gave investors tax incentives to funnel capital into revitalization projects there.

00:00:35.000 --> 00:00:39.380
These projects can serve a variety of needs, from housing to business investments.

00:00:39.500 --> 00:00:43.420
But one of the biggest opportunities is to strengthen the backbone of many of these communities:

00:00:43.420 --> 00:00:45.920
education and workforce institutions.

00:00:46.380 --> 00:00:53.580
Opportunity zone funds can finance new child care facilities, fund facilities for quality charter schools, or invest in overlooked entrepreneurs.

00:00:53.760 --> 00:00:58.960
This program is the largest community -development initiative in a generation, but its success isn't guaranteed.

00:00:59.100 --> 00:01:05.300
Community leaders, policymakers, and philanthropies will have to work together to make these investments pay off for their communities

00:01:06.460 --> 00:01:09.420
Have you heard about any opportunity zone projects in your neighborhood?

00:01:09.580 --> 00:01:14.429
Let us know in our poll, and also let us know what other topics you'd like our scholars to cover in 60

00:01:14.500 --> 00:01:19.400
Seconds, and be sure to LIKE and subscribe for more research and videos from AEI.

